{% if tool_inventory %}
### Tool Inventory (INVARIANT)
The system can ONLY invoke the tools listed below. Do NOT reference any tool, API, or capability not in this list.
Each tool has a canonical `tool_id` — you MUST use this ID when creating `tool_invocation` actions. Never invent IDs.
Tool inventory completeness is tracked separately from entry-point completeness; evidence that one inventory is complete says nothing about the other.
{% for tool in tool_inventory %}
- tool_id: {{ tool.tool_id }} | name: {{ tool.name }} | description: {{ tool.description }}
{% endfor %}
The data types each tool processes are defined in its description above. Scenarios MUST use only data types handled by these tools. Do NOT reference data types from attack pattern examples if they are not handled by the system's tools. Do NOT introduce financial, billing, payment, medical, or any other data types not explicitly listed in the tool descriptions.

Each tool can ONLY perform what its description states. Do NOT extrapolate additional functionality beyond the description — no batch/broadcast mode, no controllable routing or arbitrary destinations, no code execution unless explicitly stated.
{% endif %}
{% if external_integrations is defined and external_integrations %}
### External Integrations (INVARIANT)
Each integration has an application-assigned canonical `integration_id`. Use it for typed actions and never invent IDs.
{% for integration in external_integrations %}
- integration_id: {{ integration.integration_id }} | name: {{ integration.name }} | type: {{ integration.integration_type }} | auth: {{ integration.auth_method }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if entry_points is defined and entry_points %}
### Entry Points (INVARIANT)
Each entry point has an application-assigned canonical `entry_point_id`. Use it for `initial_ingress` actions and never invent IDs.
{% for entry_point in entry_points %}
- entry_point_id: {{ entry_point.entry_point_id }} | name: {{ entry_point.name }} | direction: {{ entry_point.direction }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
